From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: identify the existing exact O82 VRR floor interface

Expose the ABI1 marker already required by the packaged saved-floor loader.
The marker is read-only with no setter. Preserve the zero default, parser,
board/receiver/atomic admission and actual connector capability calculation.
Only an explicit existing boot/profile preference enables the VRR path.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -255,5 +255,19 @@
 	"Unqualified O82-42 receiver experiment; 0 disables, 30-143 Hz floor, OEM modes only");
 
+/* Custom parameter callbacks must publish their type explicitly. */
+__MODULE_PARM_TYPE(o82_vrr_test_min_hz, "uint");
+
+/* ABI marker consumed by the existing saved-floor module loader. */
+static unsigned int o82_vrr_floor_api = 1;
+static const struct kernel_param_ops o82_vrr_api_ops = {
+	.get = param_get_uint,
+};
+module_param_cb(o82_vrr_floor_api, &o82_vrr_api_ops,
+		&o82_vrr_floor_api, 0444);
+__MODULE_PARM_TYPE(o82_vrr_floor_api, "uint");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(o82_vrr_floor_api,
+	"Read-only O82 exact requested-floor interface version");
+
 static u32 dither_matrix[DITHER_MATRIX_SZ] = {
 	15, 7, 13, 5, 3, 11, 1, 9, 12, 4, 14, 6, 0, 8, 2, 10
 };
